  "knowledge_gaps": [
    "Suffix augmentation also reweights supervision toward later positions: for a history of length n, position j survives with probability 0.5 + 0.5j/n. Its benefit could reflect target weighting rather than removal of stale context. Add a matched loss-mask control that retains full context.",
    "The baseline receptive field is unspecified. Removing history outside that field cannot affect a prediction. Report effective context lengths and how often augmentation removes accessible context; clarify that full-history inference remains bounded by the receptive field.",
    "Negative sampling needs an explicit user-ID mapping, efficient exclusion procedure, and fallback when fewer than eight eligible items exist. The diagnostic loader's leading None cannot provide user identity. Filtering all training positives also excludes items occurring after an intermediate training target; document this choice and its effect on sampling.",
    "Global averaging over surviving positions and averaging within each row produce different training weights. Specify reduction, zero-valid-target handling, padding masks throughout convolution blocks, and B×L×8 scoring without changing the diagnostic interface.",
    "Four configurations require sixteen category-model fits. Concrete trial allocations, stopping rules, tie handling, and diagnostic reserves are missing. Report paired category-level validation differences where supported; acknowledge validation selection bias and uncertainty from only 200 users per category.",
    "Originality 4 is reasonable, but potential 7 is speculative and difficulty 4 may underestimate efficient sampling and masking. Verify the NextItNet citation title and add directly relevant cropping-augmentation references before asserting novelty."
  ],
  "follow_up_queries": [
    {
      "reason": "Distinguish context removal from recency-weighted supervision and assess whether suffix augmentation adds anything within NextItNet's receptive field.",
      "query": "Sequential recommendation training sequence cropping recent suffix augmentation NextItNet causal dilated convolutions receptive field: what prior studies compare cropping with matched target-position loss weighting, and how do they control removed context, retained target count, and full-history inference mismatch?"
    },
    {
      "reason": "Resolve implementation and objective ambiguities before treating eight-negative classification as a reproducible, inexpensive change.",
      "query": "Sequential recommendation sampled softmax uniform negatives without replacement excluding all user training positives: how do eight-negative uncorrected classification objectives differ from proposal-corrected softmax, how are repeated interactions and future-within-training positives handled, and what efficient exclusion algorithms avoid rejection-sampling stalls?"
    },
    {
      "reason": "Support reliable comparison under the fixed validation sample and shared compute budget without changing the host evaluator.",
      "query": "Recommender sampled evaluation HR@10 with 99 negative candidates and 200 users per dataset: what are the limitations of paired user bootstrap confidence intervals, repeated checkpoint and hyperparameter selection on fixed candidates, and extrapolating sampled ranking improvements to full-catalog recommendation?"
    }
